  "question": {
    "text": "Let the Mean and Variance of five observations $x_1=1, x_2=3, x_3=a, x_4=7$ and $x_5=b, a \\gt b$, be 5 and 10 respectively. Then the Variance of the observations $n+x_n, n=1,2, \\ldots \\ldots . .5$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5feEB",
      "text": "$17$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vp5K6",
      "text": "$16.4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nIQdx",
      "text": "$17.4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "trAre",
      "text": "$16$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\bar{x}=\\frac{\\sum x_i}{n}=\\frac{1+3+a+7+b}{5}=5 \\\\ & a+b=14 \\\\ & \\sigma^2=\\frac{\\sum x_i^2}{n}-(\\bar{x})^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{1^2+3^2+a^2+7^2+b^2}{5}-25=10 \\\\ & a^2+b^2=116 \\\\ & a \\gt b \\quad a=10 \\quad b=4 \\\\ & n+x_n: 2,5,13,11,9\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\sigma^2=\\frac{2^2+5^2+13^2+11^2+9^2}{5}-\\left(\\frac{2+5+13+11+9}{5}\\right)^2 \\\\ & =80-64=16\\end{aligned}$<br/>option 4",
    "image": null
  },
